		{
			"id":"e5f60718291a1b22",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# MCP Sampling\n\n**Sampling** lets an MCP server request an LLM completion *through the client* — servers have no direct access to a model. So that the server doesnt have to process the output itself. The server does its own work first, then asks the client to run a completion on its behalf: it sends a prompt, the client forwards it to Claude, and relays the generated text back for the server to use. ",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-240,
			"y":-410,
			"width":730,
			"height":200
		}
	],
